W:When this bloody war is over,
W:No more soldiering for me,
W:When I get my civvy clothes on,
W:Oh, how happy I shall be!
W:No more church parades on Sunday,
W:No more putting in for leave,
W:I shall kiss the sergeant-major,
W:How I'll miss him, how he'll grieve!
